The Digital Gift
(c) Kian Bahasadri, 2026

Upon this year of twenty-six, 
Kian's craft is in the mix.
To any soul who finds this code,
A gift is granted on the road.

Take this work and make it yours,
Open wide the digital doors.
To copy, change, or merge with skill,
To sell or license as you will.
No fee is asked, no price is set,
A freedom earned without a debt.

But heed this word, and hold it fast,
So long as these instructions last:
This scroll of rights, this name, this sign,
Must stay within each coded line.
Let every copy, part or whole,
Preserve this notice as its soul.

Yet know the truth of what is given:
By no guarantee is this engine driven.
It stands "as is," no more, no less,
To offer aid or cause a mess.
No promise here of trade or fit,
The author bears no weight of it.

If systems crash or errors fly,
No claim against the source shall lie.
For Kian rests from burden free,
Of any debt or liability.
So take the script and build your dream,
Upon this free and flowing stream.
